{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head a2610d187200f81b837aac710edd32d6bb43c265. The fix is right, and the plain test does not show that the page calls the rule, as you say. No deployed Worker or desktop AI app ran this code.\n\n**The fix.** `cardOpens` names `ready` and `incomplete`, so `stale` and any later status stay closed, and I agree with naming them over testing `!== \"unavailable\"`. `main.ts` uses the one rule at both sites, the title and `open()`, so the link and the handler cannot disagree. The cause holds: 2602c5281f wrote the condition for its unavailable placeholder, and it also took the link off an incomplete card, while the script stayed as it was. The new test holds the safety point: an incomplete card's detail lists its entries, keeps `status: incomplete`, and offers no act, so a person cannot mark as reviewed what the read did not load.\n\n**The gap you name.** I read `main.ts` and confirm that both sites call `cardOpens`, and `view-resources.test.ts` holds the rebuilt bundle. So reading and the script stand behind the page's call, and no gate does. Your open limits say so, and that is acceptable for this head.\n\n**For the planner: I agree with your recommendation.** A path-filtered CI workflow with tools installed in a scratch directory keeps `package.json` clean. A gate step that skips when its tools are missing would hide the same failure. Until the workflow exists, a head that touches `packages/mcp/browser/**`, `packages/mcp/src/views/**` or the script should run the script and cite the result. The other browser scripts stayed unrun, so each can hold a fault of this kind.\n\n**Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` is d2804590…, every digest verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's `head.txt` is 5595ddd7, exit 0, with 3533 and 1013 tests. 2fa99b16 and 5595ddd7 have the same tree, so the green run and the control apply. The red run times out at `fixture=incomplete` at main, and the green run passes 24 of 24 cases. After the gate, the head adds only the note and its manifest. I ran `view-sessions.test.ts` and `view-resources.test.ts`, `security-entry-points`, check-notes, check-doc-links and check-commit-messages, and all pass. The worktree is clean. I did not rerun the browser script or the control.\n\n**Architecture.** One small pure module, shared by the browser and a test. No hosted route changes.\n\n**Security.** An incomplete card now opens, and its detail page offers no act. Nothing that could sign is newly reachable. Your note says that no shipped source returns this state today, and I did not check that.\n\n**Simplification.** Nothing to remove.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8a1908e90df05133f1094345823ff8a175a1ea3a","binding":"assigned","head":"a2610d187200f81b837aac710edd32d6bb43c265","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5b90277fcdf85d5c28f29a0e1c47d419eeaeeca0\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f68c88cb9de59386839ba6390d0555cf7a45e54c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5b90277fcdf85d5c28f29a0e1c47d419eeaeeca0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}